# Copy to .env (gitignored, same convention as every other .env in this
# repo - see root .gitignore's "# Env" section). With NO .env at all the app
# starts in demo mode (built-in sample data, no server).
#
# A. LOCAL TESTING against your laptop: use your machine's real LAN IP - NOT
#    localhost (see services/platform.js's comment for why). Plain http is fine
#    on a home network. Example: EXPO_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_SPINE_URL=http://192.168.1.42:8001
EXPO_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_SPINE_URL=http://192.168.1.X:8001
EXPO_PUBLIC_QUOTATION_URL=http://192.168.1.X:8002
EXPO_PUBLIC_RESOURCE_NETWORK_URL=http://192.168.1.X:8003
EXPO_PUBLIC_PAYMENTS_URL=http://192.168.1.X:8004
#
# B. PRODUCTION: all four point at the same https address - your PUBLIC_DOMAIN
#    from the server's .env.prod (the gateway routes by path). You normally do
#    not edit this file for production: the "Build demo APK" GitHub workflow
#    sets these from the repository variable API_DOMAIN
#    (docs/deployment/GO-LIVE.md step 7).
#    Example: EXPO_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_SPINE_URL=https://api.yourdomain.in
#    Example: EXPO_PUBLIC_QUOTATION_URL=https://api.yourdomain.in
#    Example: EXPO_PUBLIC_RESOURCE_NETWORK_URL=https://api.yourdomain.in
#    Example: EXPO_PUBLIC_PAYMENTS_URL=https://api.yourdomain.in

# Google sign-in (optional; Android/iOS builds only, not Expo Go or web).
# WHAT:  the Client ID of a *Web application* OAuth client. A public
#        identifier. The server's GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS must contain the same value.
# WHERE: console.cloud.google.com -> APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create
#        credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Web application. In the SAME project
#        also create an "Android" client: package in.aegix.borewell + the
#        signing key's SHA-1 (printed in the APK release notes).
# Leave empty and the Google button is hidden.
# Example: EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=123456789012-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz123456.apps.googleusercontent.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=603105294808-8cqk32vc3c1kkpk25u72bi9gq17hs8ir.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Production map tiles: Geoapify's raster osm-carto style (OpenStreetMap data).
# Create a dedicated mobile-app key at https://myprojects.geoapify.com/ and
# set GEOAPIFY_API_KEY as a GitHub Actions repository VARIABLE. The workflow
# exposes it as EXPO_PUBLIC_GEOAPIFY_API_KEY at build time. For local app work,
# put the same public key in this ignored .env file:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GEOAPIFY_API_KEY=your_mobile_app_key
# Geoapify's current free plan includes 3,000 credits/day; map tiles cost 0.25
# credits each. Commercial production use is allowed within plan limits and
# required attribution must remain visible. Monitor usage in the dashboard.
#
# Optional: a custom licensed XYZ raster provider takes precedence over
# Geoapify. The app fills {z}/{x}/{y} in the URL template and shows the credit.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_TILE_URL=https://your-provider.example/{z}/{x}/{y}.png
# EXPO_PUBLIC_TILE_CREDIT=Required provider attribution
